# 3. Historical Rent Schema Validation

All historical rent tables were inspected before consolidation.

The validation identified **three distinct schema structures**.

## 3.1 Standard Rent Schema

Twenty-three municipalities used the expected structure:

```text
municipality
Studio
Studio_flag
1_Bedroom
1_Bedroom_flag
2_Bedroom
2_Bedroom_flag
3_Bedroom
3_Bedroom_flag
Total
Total_flag
Total_flag_1
```

The rent columns contain the published average monthly rent estimates.

The corresponding `_flag` columns contain CMHC reliability classifications.

---

## 3.2 East Gwillimbury Schema

The East Gwillimbury table differed from the standard structure because it did not contain:

```text
Studio
Studio_flag
```

To allow schema-compatible inspection, the missing fields were introduced as null columns during the Pandas consolidation stage.

No source values were fabricated.

Further inspection later showed that East Gwillimbury had a larger availability problem than simply missing Studio fields.

---

## 3.3 King Schema

The King historical table was structurally different from every other municipality.

Instead of rental observations, it contained only fields comparable to:

```text
Source
CMHC_Rental_Market_Survey
```

It therefore could not be interpreted as a municipality-level historical rent table.

King was excluded from the historical rent consolidation while remaining part of the project's 25-municipality geography reference.

This distinction is important:

```text
Project geography ≠ data availability
```

A municipality remains part of the project even when a specific indicator is unavailable.

---

# 4. Historical Rent Consolidation

Compatible historical tables were consolidated into a Pandas DataFrame.

King was excluded because its source did not contain comparable historical rent observations.

This resulted in:

```text
24 municipality source tables
820 wide-format historical rows
```

The raw source field labelled:

```text
municipality
```

actually contained reference periods such as:

```text
1990 October
2005 October
2025 October
```

The field was therefore renamed:

```text
reference_period
```

The actual municipality name was derived from the municipality reference table and source-table name.

Additional geographic and lineage fields were added:

```text
csd_code
municipality
region
source_table
```

This prevents the incorrectly labelled raw source field from being confused with the actual municipality.

